  "_what": "statsapi.mlb.com schedule answers read through the cors-probe workflow on a GitHub runner on 2026-10-31 (outbox/cors-result-20261031T154058Z.txt, ...T154211Z.txt, ...T154334Z.txt, ...T154431Z.txt). scripts/check-nba-board.mjs (the MLB reader and the MLB generator runs) drives the generator MLB read from these. The sandbox cannot reach statsapi, which is why a runner read them.",
  "_why_these": "off_day is a day with no games: HTTP 200, dates [], totalGames 0 - the clean empty answer the winter window must read as. game_day is the last game day of 2026 (World Series, Brewers at Rays, 2026-10-28), the full body the generator parses with the same query string it sends. error_invalid_date is what statsapi answers for a bad date: HTTP 400, no dates key. week_totalgames records that dates[i].totalGames equalled games.length on all 7 days of a regular-season week (94 games, no doubleheader in it), which is observed but NOT used by the reader: a doubleheader day was not observed.",
